# Socomec DIRIS A-40.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Socomec DIRIS A-40 — Modbus / JBUS register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: Socomec "DIRIS A-40 v1.7.4 communication table" (Power Monitoring AC
# | real-time block @ 0x4804 and Energy AC block @ 0x4D80). Read with FC03.
# | - Multi-register values are Big-Endian (most-significant word first), the
# | Socomec default — `word_order` defaults to "be" and is omitted.
# | - Manual "value weight" is folded into `scale`:
# | V x10^-2 -> 0.01    mA -> 0.001    mHz -> 0.001
# | PF /1000 -> 0.001   THD % /100 -> 0.01     W / var / VA -> 1 (raw)
# | Active energy counts in kWh, apparent in kVAh and reactive in kvarh
# | (manual weight varh x10^3) — represented directly in those units (no scale).
# | - Addresses are the protocol addresses, in decimal (e.g. 0x4804 = 18436).
# | - Factory defaults: device address (slave) = 5, RTU = 9600 baud (check unit).
# | 
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Socomec
@model=DIRIS A-40
@vendor_website=socomec.com
@description=Multifunction power monitoring device — V/I/P/Q/S per phase and system, power factor, frequency, THD and energy meters (scaled U32/S32, BE).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/socomec-diris-a40.toml; Source: Socomec "DIRIS A-40 v1.7.4 communication table" (Power Monitoring AC. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

